UPDATE scholarships SET is_active = false, application_status = 'closed', award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = NULL, award_basis = NULL, living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = NULL, tuition_coverage = NULL, english_requirements = NULL, required_documents = NULL, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = NULL, notes = $note$RETIRED on 2026-10-28 (cleanup pass 115) as a duplicate of record 51 'HKUST Admissions Scholarships for Non-Local Applicants'. This row described the same HKUST automatic academic admissions-scholarship family from the international-qualifications angle - the same 'all applicants considered automatically' channel of one-off or renewable full/partial tuition waivers, including the qualification-banded schemes (IB, GCE/International A-Level, HKDSE, Olympiad medalists) and the University Admissions Scholarship for Other Qualifications Holders - all of which record 51 covers at reliability 10 from the scheme pages fetched first-hand in pass 114, alongside the standalone records 976 (Global Learners Scholarship) and 977 (Future Leaders Award). This row additionally carried a stale funding ceiling (full tuition + HK$60,000 allowance; the current official pages read in pass 114 state HK$65,000), a nonstandard degree value (['Bachelor']) and no linked source. Its university_scholarships row 188 was deleted in this pass; HKUST's entries going forward are 51, 976 and 977.$note$, last_updated_at = now() WHERE id = 592 RETURNING id, title, is_active;

